    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval is seeking a solution to improve the efficiency of The City of Belval administrative services and quality of service rendered to users. a solution to improve the efficiency of its administrative services and quality of service rendered to users must integrate with existing practices, provide an intelligent assistance tool, and ensure continuity of file processing between agents and services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What are our company's past public sector references that align with these requirements, and how can our company's demonstrate our company's understanding of The City of Belval needs? our company's, has experience in delivering projects to the public sector." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Relevant past references include a digital workplace transformation project for the Comune di Torino, an AI-powered document management system for the Regione Lombardia, and an intelligent citizen services platform for the Métropole de Lyon." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "These projects demonstrate our company's ability to improve efficiency and quality of service in administrative contexts." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For instance, a digital workplace transformation project for the Comune di Torinoject involved a digital workplace transformation for 1200 users, which could be relevant to improving the efficiency of administrative services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The the Regione Lombardia project focused on AI-powered document management, aligning with the need for intelligent assistance tools." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To demonstrate our company's understanding of the city's needs, our company's can highlight how our company's previous projects have integrated with existing practices and ensured continuity of file processing between agents and services. our company's experience with PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies also shows that our company's are capable of managing complex public sector projects." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, our company's has a dedicated change manager and offers training delivery methods such as in-person workshops, e-learning, and quick reference guides to facilitate the adoption of new solutions by agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This capability is crucial for ensuring continuity and supporting agents during the transition to a new system." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging these past experiences and capabilities, our company's can develop a tailored solution that meets The City of Belval specific requirements and improves the efficiency of The City of Belval administrative services while providing high-quality service to users." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to provide response times compatible with daily use by agents (< 2 seconds), integrate with existing systems (business softwares, EDM, user directories) via API interfaces, and guarantee high availability (99.9%)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can our current technology stack meet these technical requirements, and what architecture do our propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, our current technology stack can meet these technical requirements as follows:  To achieve response times compatible with daily use by agents, which is less than 2 seconds, our can utilize our expertise in Cloud architecture and API integration. our have experience with cloud providers such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale (SecNumCloud), which offer scalable infrastructure to support high-performance applications." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integrating with existing systems via API interfaces, our can leverage our knowledge of API standards like REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, as well as our experience with API gateways such as Kong and Apigee. leverage will enable seamless integration with business software, Electronic Document Management (EDM) systems, and user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To guarantee high availability of 99.9%, our can design an architecture that incorporates containerization using Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm, which are all part of our containerisation expertise." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This will allow our to deploy and manage applications efficiently, ensuring minimal downtime and high uptime. our also have experience with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and the ELK stack, which can help monitor the system's performance and availability in real-time, enabling swift action in case of any issues." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of specific architecture, I propose a hybrid cloud approach where our utilize a combination of on-premise and cloud infrastructure to ensure high availability, scalability, and security." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution will be designed with a microservices architecture, allowing each component to be developed, deployed, and scaled independently. our AI/ML systems expertise can also be leveraged to implement intelligent assistance tools that can aid agents in agents daily tasks, further enhancing the overall efficiency of the system." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, by combining our technical expertise in cloud architecture, API integration, containerization, monitoring, and AI/ML systems, our can propose a robust and scalable architecture that meets the client's technical requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must respect regulatory requirements, including GDPR compliance, with data hosted exclusively in the EU, no data transfer outside the EU, and sensitive data protected through encryption or anonymization. What security controls and measures can we implement to ensure compliance with regulatory requirements, including GDPR compliance and guarantee the protection of personal data?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As a Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is well-equipped to handle GDPR compliance. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a Data Protection Officer appointed, and a Data Protection Officer appointed contact information is dpo@nexus-engineering.it." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. standard data residency policy is the EU only, which aligns with the requirement of hosting data exclusively in the EU. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To protect sensitive data, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. Additionally, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have implemented various security controls to ensure the protection of personal data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of access control, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. enforce multi-factor authentication using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. design Role-Based Access Control systems. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also utilize Privileged Access Management solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. network security architecture follows patterns such as Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems deployed and experience with DDoS mitigation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regular penetration testing is conducted annually, and after major releases, with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. last test showing 2 medium findings, which were all remediated. For AI security controls, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. protect against prompt injection, redact PII from outputs, detect adversarial inputs, and have a confidence threshold escalation process in place." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Model isolation is ensured through an inference API, preventing direct model access for end-users, and security reviews are conducted during model updates. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. audit and logging practices include logging all queries, using append-only logs with SHA-256 hash chaining for immutability, retaining audit logs for 7 years, and integrating with SIEM tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM in real-time." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the specific requirements of not transferring data outside the EU and protecting sensitive data through encryption or anonymization, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can implement data encryption at rest and in transit, ensure that all data processing activities are carried out within the EU, and use Nexus Engineering S.r.l. anonymisation tools to protect personal data. By leveraging these existing security controls and measures, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can help ensure compliance with GDPR regulations and provide robust protection for personal data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The contract requires strict GDPR compliance, explicability, and transparency of recommendations, as well as explicit validation of automated decisions by an agent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we standard contractual clauses and AI regulatory posture aligned with strict GDPR compliance, explicability, and transparency of recommendations, as well as explicit validation of automated decisions by an agent?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the provided context, I can identify that The contract requires strict GDPR compliance, explicability, and transparency of recommendations, as well as explicit validation of automated decisions by an agent.  we, has experience with GDPR legal instruments, including a standard DPA template version 3.2 and a standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) for performance of task in public interest. we also have dpia support available." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding AI regulatory posture, we have EU AI Act expertise and are aware of prohibited AI practices. we also enforce human oversight contractual enforcement and have a policy of no automated decision without human validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for legal risks, I can flag the following: open-source license compliance, cross-border data flow (although we context indicates intra-EU operations only), EU AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation through source code escrow and open standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, given the requirements, the primary focus should be on ensuring GDPR compliance, explicability, and transparency in AI-driven recommendations, as well as adhering to the principle of human validation for automated decisions. we standard contractual clauses include a data return on termination clause within 30 days and a data destruction certificate. we also prioritize client data ownership, stating that all client data remains the sole property of the contracting authority." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of alignment with the requirements, we posture seems to address the key concerns through we GDPR compliance measures, AI regulatory awareness, and emphasis on human validation for automated decisions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, it is crucial to ensure that we standard contractual clauses and AI regulatory posture are explicitly aligned with the contract's specific requirements regarding explicability, transparency, and explicit validation of automated decisions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, with annual operating costs to be controlled and compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities. Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

